<Layout
	title="THE ORIGIN OF ANALOGIUM"
	pubDate={new Date('March 10 2023')}
	heroImage="/FATHER_dark.jpg"
>
	<h1>PART I: One-Man Show</h1>
	<p>
		Our society was born from an entity in constant pain, a human being like you or me, with a life
		so miserable that it is "forgettable"; he fled for a long time in his own mind, thinking and
		dreaming of new worlds and alternate histories to those of our world. Eventually he made the
		decision to archive and share these worlds that gave him so much fear and comfort over the years,
		that's how <b>ANALOGIUM</b> was born... yet is not the end of our story.
	</p><p>
		Although the project filled our <i>founding father</i> with life, the work was too much and soon,
		along with private events, took its toll on his mental state. He knew he needed help, but all the
		time he spent locked in his own dome ended his ability to go out and talk to other humans. He became
		a hermit, and finding someone as fallen and broken as he was was practically impossible... until <i>she</i>
		arrived to his life.
	</p>

	<h1>PART II: From Bliss to Feeling Half-Death</h1>
	<p>
		"Lady" was everything to our creator, she was the only person in a long time to understand and heal the
		creator's mental wounds. He himself described her as "a fallen angel". But unfortunately nothing good can
		last for anyone, and one day "Lady" evaporated from our father's life. This left him completely devastated,
		he didn't smile, he didn't see, he didn't move, he was just present, <b>lifeless</b>.
	</p><p>
		Nobody knows for sure what broke our founder's fairytale, not even the ones closest to him; the only
		thing he allows himself to say is <i>"<a href="/FAULT.png" class="logo toggleable">It was my fault</a>"</i>.
	</p>

	<h1>PART III: Among Ashes</h1>
	<p>
		It took a long time for our founder to heal, full of empty replacements, insane acts and feelings amplified
		by his own pain; until in a monument of clarity, the stories that had locked him in his mind for so long resounded in
		his mind, and he found something that made him happy again, however temporary it seemed. He worked as hardly as he could
		but at last, he felt whole. Now our founding father was not alone, he managed to find a team that had the same mind as him.
		He found a family.
	</p>
</Layout>
